{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components for every k (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k, the maximal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sets of vertices whose induced subgraph has more than k vertices and no vertex cut of fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices. Parallel edges count once and self-loops not at all."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Level 1 is the connected components with an edge and level 2 the blocks of three or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices. Each higher level refines each component of the level below: vertices of fewer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than k neighbors are peeled off, and each piece left is either k-connected or split by a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex cut X of fewer than k vertices into parts D, each searched again as D ∪ X. A cut is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"found by Even’s method, unit-capacity flows on the split network between each of k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices and every later one it is not adjacent to, each stopped after k augmenting paths.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m) for levels 1 and 2; each refinement at level k makes at most k n"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flows of O(k (n + m)) each."}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kcomponents()"]}],"metadata":{"title":"kComponents()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"KComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/KComponents.swift#L80","fileName":"KComponents.swift"},"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P12ConnectivityE11kComponentsAD11KComponentsVyxGyF","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Connectivity"}]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/kComponents()":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kcomponents()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kComponents()","type":"topic","title":"kComponents()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components for every k (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k, the maximal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sets of vertices whose induced subgraph has more than k vertices and no vertex cut of fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices. Parallel edges count once and self-loops not at all."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV","text":"KComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/KComponents":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KComponents","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"KComponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"Connectivity","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity","role":"collection"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","title":"Graph","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"abstract":[],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"}}}